 "about": "Signed Tempo transactions and key authorizations given to a local Tempo node (ghcr.io/tempoxyz/tempo:latest, Tempo 1.19.0-dev f80ab3c7, dev chain 1337, genesis cut so that T14 is active) on 2026-11-22, with what the node did: `included` (eth_sendRawTransaction took it and its receipt names `account` as the sender; for a key authorization, the account keychain then held the key for `account`) or `rejected`. `control/valid-single-key` and `single/key-authorization(wallet)` are signed by a single-key account (secp256k1, 65 bytes). Every other `account` is a configurable account (T14), whose signatures are type 0x05: upgraded in place to one secp256k1 owner (k1), two owners at threshold 2 (k2of2), one P256 owner (p256), one WebAuthn owner (webauthn), and one never a single-key account, its address derived from its configuration (initial). `design/forged-0x05-naming-another-account` is a 0x05 signature naming an account whose owners did not sign it; the node rejected it. Recorded by the round-5 trial t14-signature-closure (out/bytes-t14@0.17.6.json, seed round-5) and copied here unchanged.",
